T:Steps for
T:CPR
T:
T:1.
T:Check your
T:surroundings
T:for any 
T:threats
T:2.
T:Wake person
T:to test for
T:a response
T:3.
T:Call 911 and
T:tell someone
T:nearby to 
T:find an AED
T:4.
T:Lay person
T:flat and 
T:kneel
T:beside them
T:5.
T:Push to at 
T:least 2 
T:inches but
T:no more than
T:2.4 inches 
T:6.
T:Do this 30
T:times with
T:push, then
T:tilt head 
T:back and
T:put your 
T:mouth on 
T:theirs.
T:Blow into
T:them once,
T:take a 
T:breath, 
T:then blow 
T:again.
T:7. 
T:Continue the 
T:cycle until
T:AED or EMS
T:arrives.
T:Apply sticky
T:pads and
T:follow its 
T:prompts.
T:You MUST 
T:take cloths
T:off to
T:apply sticky
T:pads. Do not
T:feel
T:embarressed.
T:YOU are 
T:SAVING
T:someone's
T:life.
T:8.
T:ONLY if the 
T:AED says so,
T:step away
T:from the 
T:person and 
T:hit the 
T:shock button
T:9.
T:Continue
T:your CPR
T:cycle.
T:Until EMS 
T:arrives and 
T:takes over.
T:
T:
